      "message": "Thanks for review.\n\nCurrent state:\n\nEntity-Manager owns the GPU chassis board object path, and that object path hosts the Item.Chassis / Item.Board interfaces.\n\nGpuSensor resolves that EM board object path via the endpoint\u0027s configured_by association, then calls add_interface() on that same object path to publish:\n\nCommon.UUID\nDecorator.PowerBounds\nDecorator.SKU\nDecorator.LocationCode\nConnector.Slot\n\nSo a single object path carries interfaces from two services — EM the identity interfaces, GpuSensor the attribute interfaces — with no association in between.\nI\u0027d like to make sure I\u0027ve understood your point correctly — would this be the co-owned pattern you\u0027re referring to?\n\nOr should GpuSensor instead publish these attribute interfaces on its own object path (never touching EM\u0027s path), and use Association.Definitions (contained_by / containing) to link its own object path to the EM chassis object path — with bmcweb reading GpuSensor\u0027s attributes by following that association? That way every object path has a single owner and EM\u0027s path is never modified by another service.\n\nThank you very much for the guidance.",
